I've been playing nethack off/on for a few months now. Honestly, I
never really took it seriously until about a week ago. I'd play like an
idiot, quaff from every fountain I saw, and always attack. I always
went straight into the mines, most characters died before Minetown, and
none of them made it until Mine's End.

Enter Miael, my new Valkyrie, one of the first ones I made. I tore
through the first few levels.

However, on the way, which defined most of my game, I ate a tengu, and
got teleportitis. I didn't see more tengus for more or less the entire
game, ruling out intrinsic TC; nor did I get a =oTC for a long time. I
made it to Minetown with Teleportitis. At this point, I was doing about
average, still; I had a decent inventory of rings and scrolls from
random drops. The altar wasn't aligned there, but, I went ahead and
BUC'd everything to check it out. I also found a pair of chests behind
locked doors, and made those my official stash. I went, tried on rings
to see what they'd do, and then I walked around with a few unID's, but
UC'd rings on.

I see the Captain of the Watch brutally murder an underling, and take
my now #name'd =oC off. I find out I have quite a bit of cursed scrolls
and wands, as I've run into several of my past bonefiles, and I was an
assiduous thief in other games. However, I don't keep notes, and I
never ID'd them in half those games anyhow, so I've got no clue what
I'm carrying around. I do, by chance, however, ID teleport scrolls from
observation, and find out I have five of them, two blessed, 1 uncursed,
1 cursed. I take the Blessed along, figuring I'm already a teleport
nut. I also go check around the shops as a last note; and, lo and
behold, I pick up some Boots of Speed. I am now very, very, very happy

I fight my way lower into the mines, and don't encounter any real
difficulty for a bit. I found some Elvish Mithril on the way down here,
so my AC is around -7, more then enough to just hack and slash through.


Until I step on a polymorph trap, and shred a load of my gear as I
become an Ettin Zombie. I then step onto a flame trap immediately after
I return to original form, and scorch my shield.

Now, I'm two levels below minetown, my gear is worse then when I
stepped in the dungeon, I figure I'm dead already and keep plunging
through.

I somehow make it to the Wine Cellar version of Mine's End anyhow.
Looking back on it, I frequently teleported without control out of
dangerous situations, because I kept charging into them. It let me
string out masses of enemies, rather then face them all at once. I also
kept finding potions of healing. I get the luckstones, the potions of
water and so on, and I head back up to Minetown.

I go to work here, playing with my stash for a bit, before I head back
into the Dungeons of Doom.

I find a leprechaun hall and an altar, which I swiftly convert, on the
next floor. I also eat a floating eye here, although I lack a
blindfold. I do, however, have a =oSI that I got in the mines, which I
wear to hunt down leprechauns.

I head back to Minetown. I get some scrolls of create monster, several
of which are cursed, and head back to the altar, thinking Mjollnir or
bust.

Sure enough, I get one after I'm forced to switch to my first cursed
scroll. I go down further, and hit Sokoban. Here, I don't use spoilers;
instead, I solve it through logic, and fight my way to the Amulet of
Reflection. I also find not one, but two magic markers here. I decide
it's time to go to work.

I lack a wand of cancellation, so I head back to minetown, and start
#dipping various items in the Minetown fountains. I had accidentally
teleported out of a shop with a pancake before, and between =oC and
Mjollnir, I had obliterated the watch. I summon two water demons while
here; the first, I clean his clock in short order.

The second decided I need a wish. I consider, and think about how
burdened I've been the entire game, and that I have reflection but am
more or less good, for now. One Blessed Fixed Bag of Holding later, and
with a lot of fun with Magic Markers and Holy Water, my inventory is
looking pretty good, although I'm missing the items considered
essential for moving down in the dungeon past Medusa and so on.

I then go and read a few Blessed ?IDs, and soon identify my entire
inventory, including gems from the mines. I bankrupt every store I've
seen that accepts gems thus far, and buy protection to AC 0. I also
stuff various wands and scrolls away; none of them are too spectacular.
I have a few of light, a few digging, a few lightning, but, no wishing,
no polymorph, no scrolls of charging or genocide.

I resume my dive through the dungeon, Mjollnir'ing everything in my
path without breaking a sweat. A few levels down, I gain a =oTC: Now, I
tear through the dungeon, frequently flashing around enemies and back
to essential points. I abuse this like crazy, in short, and tear
through everything in sight. My boots of speed happened to be Snow
Boots; thus, I don't see any real issues, having long since gained
resist fire and shock intrinsics. I do run into an issue on the second
level; until I find a Blessed Potion of Levitation next to me. I then
float over, and go greet Lord Surtur. I lack a safe way to cover the
Drawbridges at first, then my long-inactive teleportitis comes up
again, and thanks to =oTC, I jump right next to Surtur over the lava,
and pound away. He flees to the upstairs, and I teleport over the lava;
he flees again, and I tear him to shreds when he runs out of places to
run. I now have the Orb of Fate.


I find a throneroom a few levels down; I see no less then five dragons
here. I pick up several sets of scales here, and, guess what? One of
them is grey. I slap it on. At this point, my gear is as follows: +0
GDSM, +1 Dwarvish Iron Helm, +0 Leather Gloves, +0 Boots of Speed, +3
Burnt Small Shield, +0 Oilskin Cloak/+1 Elvish Cloak (I kept the
Oilskin in my BoH) Blessed +2 Mojo, AoR, =oTC and =oFA/C/SI (Depends on
what's needed - I switched the ring around frequently.) I had also, on
my way down, identified Strangulation for kicks, mostly. It was with
this gear, that I reached Fort Ludios. I used both my scrolls of earth
from Sokoban here, made a bridge, got inside. I didn't run into any
serious opponents here; I did, however, store up on rations. Nothing
eventful happened here, honestly; aside from angering my god, possibly
through excessive praying after crowning, but, with the gold from
Ludios, I rebought protection. Next was Medusa.

I still lacked any form of Levitation. At this point, I had everything
else I'd need, really, but I still lacked Levitation, which really got
on my nerves. I took out my pickaxe, dug down to the castle. I then put
on my blindfold, walked back up the stairs, and brutally murdered
Medusa. Perseus' statue had some Boots of Levitation, which I promptly
uncursed. I then walked back down to the castle, and realized I had on
me no wands of striking, nor did I have Force Bolt. Instead of opening
the drawbridge, then, I went in and entered from the rear. I fell down
one of the trapdoors and wound up in the Valley of the Dead, and
immediately ran the hell back up. I panicked for a moment there, then
kept the boots of levitation on as I crossed the next four trapdoors.
Took off the Levitation, put on Speed, put on Conflict.

I walked into absolute chaos, as the various monsters, including an
arch-lich who ran afoul of a black dragon before he got near me,
started massacring each other. One guard whipped out a uranium wand,
and shot a death ray at me, that bounced off my AoR. Also, somewhere in
here, someone had their life saved; thus, I figured out the other
cursed amulet I had was, in fact, an Amulet of Life Saving, not
something unpleasant. After plowing through it all, and reaching the
Wand of Wishing, I paused for a moment. I ID'd it as 0:3, and I
wondered what to get. I started out with a pair of blessed scrolls of
Charging, the first I'd ever seen. I also wished up some Gauntlets of
Power, a Shield of Reflection, and here I paused for a moment. For my
fourth wish, after a recharge, I got a Wand of Cancellation. For my
fifth wish,  I wished for 'Genocid' first and got two blessed ID
instead, wasting a wish. For my sixth, I did it right, and wishes for
two blessed Genocide, and decided to wait before wresting a wish for an
uncursed Magic Marker. I went to sit on the throne after genociding all
liches, hoping a wish or something else would come out; a few moments
later, I had the uncursed Magic Marker, and had genocided all Green
Slimes, to boot.

Now, I thought. I wondered what else I would want to genocide. I was
using a Shield of Reflection and had MR, so that changed my game a bit,
as I could wear an Oilskin Cloak instead. That meant I had no need,
really, to genocide ;. I also thought a helmet meant immunity to master
mind flayers, after running into a few normal ones. Bad idea, although
I wouldn't figure this out until too late. I enchanted up all my armor
to +4 and +5, Mojo to +6, checked my three amulets of Life Saving, and
went down into the VotD. I'm level 15 by this point, by the way; I was
levelling solely from Wraith Corpses and potions of Gain Level.
Gehennom provided no real issues; I picked up another amulet of life
saving in Vlad's tower, but, nothing gave me any real problems.
Asmodeus and Baelzbub both got paid off, Juiblex engulfed me and died a
few turns later from the Big Hammer, and Orcus wasn't a real threat at
all. I dropped through a few trapdoors, then, and saw the Wizard of
Yendor through telepathy, and went nuts running around Gehennom and
wondered where I screwed up. A thousand turns later, I realized that,
in fact, nothing was wrong. It was my first time in Gehennom, after
all, and randomly appearing on his floor threw me off until I read a
Magic Mapping. I went all the way down, found the Vibrating Square, cut
paths through Gehennom between stairs, and got ready to go to work.
Rodney dodged the first death ray, but not the second. I had 3 charges
left, now. I ran down to the VS without seeing him, performed the
invocation ritual, started chopping through here. As a note here, I
encountered Yeeonghu. I kept smashing him with Mojo, he kept running
away, but, I kept my eyes on the sanctum, and kept searching for the
door. I then got inside, only to find - There was no High Priestess, at
all. I wondered for a moment what the hell was going on; needless to
say, there was no amulet, either. I deduced that somehow (I still don't
know how), Yeeonghu wound up with it. I chased him back to the
upstairs, and found him there. I started smashing.

He summoned Demogorgon, who I didn't recognize at all, until I had been
hit with TWO sickness attacks. Then I stopped for a moment, looked up a
spoiler on him. I deduced that I had three actions. Less if he hit me
again. I needed to get the hell away, now. I zapped him with a wand of
teleport, ran up the stairs, and realized that I was going to lose an
amulet of life saving - But being Very Fast saved me, and I had just
enough time to apply my blessed unicorn horn and cure my sickness. More
importantly, I left Demogorgon on the bottom floor, which I would never
return to again. I chased down Yeeonghu, two floors up, and found an
Amulet of Yendor on him. I took it, ID'd it to make sure (I have a
friend who, two days before I ascended, ascended with a fake amulet),
and then #name'd it. I started running up to the next set of stairs -
then Rodney came, and summoned nasties. I hit him with another charge
from the /oD.

...But the Master Mind Flayer hit me with Amnesia.

This was bad, and I thought this ascension run was over. I had about a
dozen levels of Gehennom to go through, then the dungeons of doom,
where I would have to re-explore some levels. Either way, I took my
chance, and ran.

My teleportitis + teleport control, above all else, is what saved me. I
skipped about a dozen levels here through sake of that; Rodney appeared
a few more times, but, he didn't steal my quest artifact, double
trouble, or evensummon nasties more then once, and that time, I /oD'd
him and got an instant teleport which took me off the level. I made my
way to the top, and just for fun, stood on the upstairs and quaffed one
of my two cursed potions of gain level. I /oD'd Rodney one last time,
and realized I had one charge left. I then took inventory - I had three
scrolls of Gold Detection, one Genocide, a Magic Mapping. I also had a
few trash scrolls, and no more magic marker charges. I confused myself
casting Divine Monster, and read one of the Magic Mapping scrolls. No
problem here, or with the plane of fire.

Air, I realized, was an issue. I kept getting swallowed. Mojo was not
the same hammer it usually was here. I quickly gave up at smashing all
the elementals and monsters first, and just ran for the portal like I
had on Earth.

Water, I was out of Gold Detection scrolls. However, with an Oilskin
cloak, and Conflict/Free Action rings, and Boots of Levitation, I
essentially genocided the whole level - there were four monsters left
in the entire level, one of which was peaceful, when I got on the
Astral Plane.

I had one charge in the wand of death, which I thought would be
sufficient. I had telepathy, which I used extensively. And I had a Ring
of Conflict. I decided to save the /oD, as it had been charged once - I
regretted not wresting a second /oD out of my exhausted Wand of Wishing
here. As was, I started going to work on the plane and the riders.
Pestilence, first: I just took him down once with the hammer, and I
wanted to save my /oD for Famine. I'd throw Mojo at death, in my mind.
With this said, I moved back a bit, to get Death in a good straight
line.

And the Pestilence came up behind me, and I died taking him out a
second time - Fortunately, I had an amulet of life saving. I slapped
another one on, and I saw and hammered Pestilence a third time, before
I realized what was going on.

I had killed him thrice. They respawned, and I didn't know. I figured I
had worked past Amnesia, I could get past this. I immediately dashed
towards Famine, and hit him with the /oD. I went in, and, luckily - The
altar was aligned. I did the n00b dance of putting the amulet on the
altar, then did it right and offered it up. Ascended I did!


